== Their relationship ==

The Four Foundations investigate the philosophical questions beneath the undertaking. The Manifesto articulates its direction and necessity. The Constitution expresses the commitments by which BITwiki pursues that direction and protects intellectual sovereignty.

The superseded Charter is preserved in repository Git history for provenance and study, not as a separate governing instrument.

'''The four philosophical foundations are not the four conditions examined in the Manifesto.''' They address different questions and should remain conceptually distinct.

These writings are meant to be read together. Their roles differ, but their purpose is shared: to make BITwiki's direction, reasoning, responsibilities, and enduring commitments intelligible to the people who encounter, study, and develop it.

